<html lang="en">
<head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Skeleton inspection</title><style>:root{font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;color:#243744;background:#f3f6f8;font-size:15px}*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0}header,main{max-width:1400px;margin:auto;padding:24px}header{padding-bottom:4px}h1{font-size:32px;margin:8px 0}h2{font-size:18px;margin:6px 0 12px}.eyebrow{letter-spacing:.12em;font-size:12px;color:#267282;font-weight:700}p{line-height:1.5}.controls,.transport,.legend{display:flex;gap:14px;align-items:end;flex-wrap:wrap}.controls{margin:10px 0 18px}label{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px;font-weight:600;font-size:13px}select,input,button{font:inherit;border:1px solid #b3c2cb;border-radius:7px;padding:9px;background:white;color:inherit}button{cursor:pointer}button:hover{background:#e1edf0}#play{background:#145e73;color:white;min-width:80px}#frame{flex:1;min-width:160px;padding:0;align-self:center}output{min-width:215px;align-self:center;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}#status{padding:10px 14px;border-radius:6px;background:#e0eaf0;min-height:44px}.panels{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:20px}.card{background:white;border:1px solid #d5e0e6;border-radius:12px;padding:20px;margin-bottom:20px;min-width:0}canvas{width:100%;display:block}#pose{aspect-ratio:800/660}#separation,#relative{aspect-ratio:800/275}.legend span{margin-right:12px}.raw{color:#176d8a}.filtered{color:#d07326}.com{color:#14804a}.foot{color:#995da0}.card p,aside{font-size:13px;color:#526772}.inline{flex-direction:row;align-items:center;margin-top:-5px}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:12px}#note{min-width:250px}aside{padding:4px 12px}@media(max-width:850px){.panels{grid-template-columns:1fr}header,main{padding:14px}h1{font-size:25px}.controls{gap:10px}select{max-width:100%}.card{padding:12px}#note{min-width:0;width:100%}}
</style></head>
<body>
<header><p class="eyebrow">PINN FALL RESEARCH · RECORDING INSPECTION</p><h1 id="title">Skeleton inspection</h1><p id="context"></p></header>
<main>
<section class="controls">
<label>Trial<select id="trial"></select></label>
<label>Display<select id="mode"><option value="raw">Raw</option><option value="filtered">Filtered</option><option value="overlay">Raw + filtered</option></select></label>
<label>Camera projection<select id="view"><option value="xy">X / −Y</option><option value="xz">X / Z</option><option value="yz">Z / −Y</option></select></label>
<label>Playback speed<select id="speed"><option value="0.25">0.25×</option><option value="0.5">0.5×</option><option value="1" selected>1×</option></select></label>
</section>
<section class="transport"><button id="previous" aria-label="Previous frame">← Frame</button><button id="play">Play</button><button id="next" aria-label="Next frame">Frame →</button><button id="nextFlag">Next flagged/repaired frame</button><input type="range" id="frame" min="0" value="0" aria-label="Frame"><output id="time"></output></section>
<p id="status" role="status"></p>
<div class="panels"><section class="card"><h2>Skeleton and CoM proxy</h2><canvas id="pose" width="800" height="660"></canvas><p class="legend"><span class="raw">● Raw</span><span class="filtered">● Filtered</span><span class="com">● CoM proxy</span><span class="foot">◆ Foot midpoint</span></p><p>One fixed initial-pelvis origin per trial. Equal spatial scale; dotted foot connection shows landmark geometry, not ground contact.</p></section>
<section class="card"><h2>Foot separation · camera X/Z</h2><canvas id="separation" width="800" height="275"></canvas><h2>CoM relative to foot midpoint</h2><label class="inline">Coordinate<select id="traceAxis"><option value="0">Camera X</option><option value="1">Camera −Y</option><option value="2">Camera Z</option></select></label><canvas id="relative" width="800" height="275"></canvas><p>Traces are in metres against nominal seconds. The current frame is marked; peach shading shows raw audit flags and purple shading shows repaired frames.</p></section></div>
<section class="card"><h2>Manual phase notes</h2><p>Record provisional observations from skeleton playback. These are not video-confirmed contacts or automatic event labels. Export notes before closing this page.</p><div class="controls"><label>Phase<select id="phase"><option value="initial_standing">Initial standing</option><option value="fall_onset">Fall onset</option><option value="descent">Descent</option><option value="apparent_contact">Apparent contact</option><option value="post_fall">Post-fall movement</option></select></label><label>Observation<input id="note" placeholder="Optional observation"></label><button id="mark">Mark this frame</button><button id="exportNotes">Export notes JSON</button><button id="clearNotes">Clear notes</button></div><pre id="notes">No phase notes recorded.</pre></section>
<aside><strong>Interpretation</strong><p id="filterInfo"></p><p>Camera coordinates only. No calibrated floor height, contact-based BoS, forces or instability labels are inferred. Repaired-frame markings, raw repeats and review flags remain visible in every mode. Filtering does not repair the recording; the separately documented gap-repair step created the inspected numeric inputs.</p></aside>
